  "adaptations": [
    "Reuse the original Gaussian material/profiles/gains and four cloth zones plus 32 close bands. Default patch output remains exact at the tested replay times.",
    "Add explicit per-patch authoritative presentation age and a pool reset; do not copy private fixture lifetime, wind bake, point light or HDR renderer into production.",
    "Fit goat/horse effects to their native clothing dimensions without changing model scale, vertices, UVs, materials, skeletons or equipment.",
    "Track fitted bands through native skin transforms; cloth tips retain the original barycentric posed-triangle method and measured outward offset.",
    "Inspect only the existing tagged Chicago outfit for visible replacement cloth. Exclude hidden replaced garments, helmets, badges, weapons and metal.",
    "Preserve the accepted flat adapter API. Coder maps characterFire into active/startedAt/intensity after poses and elevation; source physics is never inspected.",
    "Angular onset is a deterministic actor-ID visual default, not a claimed gameplay impact or mesh-hit result.",
    "Final code adds explicit unsupported-binding diagnostics after the visual capture. Exact supported splat data matches the preserved captured source across four bodies and five times."
  ],
